 #### DYNAISOLOD Geometry Generation
 **Definition**: A method that generates triangles on a cell-by-cell basis for cells containing the isosurface, using a modified (disambiguated) triangulation table similar to Marching Cubes [S3, unofficial].
-**Steps**: For each cell, determine which corners are above or below the isovalue to identify intersecting edges. Use the modified triangulation table to decide how to triangulate the isosurface within the cell. Calculate vertex positions by linearly interpolating along the intersecting cell edges. Store calculated vertices in a hash table keyed by the edge they lie on to avoid redundant calculations. Compute normals for each triangle using a cross-product and store them in the same hash table. Optionally, use the hash table to arrange adjacent triangles into triangle strips for more compact representation [S3, unofficial].
